                <pb facs="1209" n="1191" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg1191"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">834.34/3–2246: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Beaulac</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-03-27T20:00:00-05:00">March 27, 1946—8 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>63. Before giving its approval Dept wishes your recommendation on Navy Dept
                    proposal to sell to Paraguay from surplus 18 landing craft of assorted sizes and
                    types armed with small guns and suitable for river transportation of personnel
                    and vehicles. These small vessels requested by Paraguay in staff conversations,
                    and constitute Navy interim program for Paraguay. Similar allocations being made
                    to several other countries including Uruguay, Peru, Ecuador, Chile.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
